    * Copilot Studio and Agent-workflow synthesis
        * Eg. In the first pattern, a Power Automate workflow provides the rigid, auditable framework for a business process, managing handoffs, branching logic, and system writes. When the process encounters a step requiring cognitive judgment—such as extracting data from inconsistently formatted supplier contracts—the workflow calls an "Agent Node". This node executes an inline or pre-configured agent, utilizing Work IQ to ground the model in the user’s Microsoft 365 context (including Teams, Outlook, and SharePoint) to complete the cognitive task before returning control to the deterministic workflow
        * Eg.  How it handles high-stake task? In the second pattern, an autonomous agent handling an open-ended request invokes a cloud workflow as a tool to execute a high-stakes transaction safely. To protect system integrity, the workflow must meet strict structural constraints: it must begin with a "When an agent calls the flow" trigger, end with a "Respond to the agent" action, execute in real time, and return its payload within a strict 100-second window.
